OMEGA_PHASE=unprovisioned

This master image contains no site identity or credentials. Phase 5 must
create pihole.env and evebox.env, enroll Wazuh and Tailscale, set the Suricata
capture interface and HOME_NET, configure networking, and enable services.

Dashboard and local AI files are included but disabled. Before activation,
Phase 5 must provide read access to the container Pi-hole database and sensor
logs and connect a supported Wazuh manager feed. Copy dashboard-setup.json.example
to a root-owned mode-0600 private configuration, review it for this device, and
use /usr/libexec/omega/configure-dashboard --check, then --apply, with --config
pointing to that file. The helper creates a unique dashboard password,
dashboard.env, and dashboard.ready; services remain stopped. Enable them only
after owner access is configured, then verify collection and AI. The master
image must never include this marker, an active dashboard.env, passwords,
network histories, device labels, or a customer's manager connection settings.
The dashboard binds only to loopback; customer browser access is a separate
provisioning responsibility. Setup preferences do not enforce parental controls.
